<title>POLAND: Polish Gdansk refinery raises fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Polish Gdansk refinery raises fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's second largest Gdansk refinery raised on Wednesday its wholesale prices of petrol and diesel by 20 zlotys per tonne which may result in a retail price rise of two 0.02 zlotys per litre, the refinery said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the move was a result of the rise of the dollar exchange rate and fuel prices on world markets.</p>
<p>On Monday Poland's biggest Plock refinery announced it raised its petrol prices by 10 zlotys per tonne and its diesel prices by 20 zlotys per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
